x360-native local patch 0003 for rexglue-sdk f5337cdc947ff6d4c4196737e2c807a48f2a1fc2 (v0.10.0)

Imports: pair a function import's slot and thunk across the records of one
library; a function import without any thunk is a codegen validation error.

XexModule::SetupLibraryImports paired the two records of a function import
(type 0 = value slot, type 1 = thunk) by ordinal only inside one
xex2_import_library record. dash.xex 2.0.17559.0 has xam split over two
records, with the slot of xam 0x8E2 in the first and its thunk in the second.
The slot half became an import symbol at address 0 (PopulateBinaryData), the
codegen registered __imp__XamNuiGetSupportString there, and the first
PPCFuncMappings entry was { 0x0, ... }: Runtime::Setup stops at guest == 0 and
registered no recompiled function ("No function registered at 92196610").

The loader now completes the half-filled entry of an earlier record of the
same library (slot-only with thunk-only, either order) instead of keeping two
halves; entries complete on both sides, or two halves of the same kind, stay
separate. The Register phase no longer maps an import symbol at address 0: a
known function import without a thunk adds an ImportWithoutThunk analysis
error (generation is blocked unless --force), an unresolved one keeps its
"Cannot resolve ordinal" error. Variable imports are unchanged.

Test: tests/sdkcheck/import_records_test.cpp (sdkcheck.* in ctest), on a
synthetic XEX2 built by the test.
No upstream equivalent at the time of writing (development bd833a2 identical
in these functions).

